From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:04:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't take the API lock for semaphore surface
 UNREGISTER_WAITER

NV_SEMAPHORE_SURFACE_CTRL_CMD_UNREGISTER_WAITER is exported with
API_LOCK_READONLY, while its counterpart REGISTER_WAITER is NO_API_LOCK.
nvidia-drm calls it through KAPI when it re-arms a semaphore surface fence
callback (DRM_NVIDIA_SEMSURF_FENCE_CREATE, from the compositor's main thread
for explicit-sync client buffers), so it waits for every API lock writer.
Measured with a CUDA client (nvidia-vaapi-driver under ffmpeg) starting and
exiting: KWin's main thread blocked in the ioctl up to 16.8 ms, 53 ms total
over 6 cycles, behind UVM_REGISTER/UNREGISTER_CHANNEL and RM frees holding
the API lock for write.

Like REGISTER_WAITER, UNREGISTER_WAITER only touches the semaphore surface's
shared waiter map under its spinlock; the surface itself is protected by the
client lock, which is still taken. The notifier walk detaches signaled waiters
under the same spinlock before delivering them, so an unregister racing with
it just doesn't find the waiter and fails, which KAPI already handles (it
then leaves the callback to run). Export it with the same flags as
REGISTER_WAITER (NO_API_LOCK | NON_PRIVILEGED | NO_GPUS_LOCK); the
NO_API_LOCK path in _rmapiRmControl also skips the GPU access reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/generated/g_sem_surf_nvoc.c | 10 +++++-----
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c  |  8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/generated/g_sem_surf_nvoc.c b/src/nvidia/generated/g_sem_surf_nvoc.c
index e18191a4..02866b1f 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/generated/g_sem_surf_nvoc.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/generated/g_sem_surf_nvoc.c
@@ -157,11 +157,11 @@ static NV_STATUS semsurfCtrlCmdSetValue__EXPORT(void *pSemaphoreSurf, void *pPar
 }
 #endif // !NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x00000109u)
 
-#if !NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x00000109u)
+#if !NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x00400009u)
 static NV_STATUS semsurfCtrlCmdUnregisterWaiter__EXPORT(void *pSemaphoreSurf, void *pParams) {
     return semsurfCtrlCmdUnregisterWaiter_IMPL(pSemaphoreSurf, pParams);
 }
-#endif // !NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x00000109u)
+#endif // !NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x00400009u)
 
 // Exported method array
 static const struct NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DEF __nvoc_exported_method_def_SemaphoreSurface[] = 
@@ -227,12 +227,12 @@ static const struct NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DEF __nvoc_exported_method_def_Semaphor
 #endif
     },
     {               /*  [4] */
-#if NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x109u)
+#if NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x400009u)
         /*pFunc=*/      (void (*)(void)) NULL,
 #else
         /*pFunc=*/      (void (*)(void)) &semsurfCtrlCmdUnregisterWaiter__EXPORT,
-#endif // NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x109u)
-        /*flags=*/      0x109u,
+#endif // NVOC_EXPORTED_METHOD_DISABLED_BY_FLAG(0x400009u)
+        /*flags=*/      0x400009u,
         /*accessRight=*/0x0u,
         /*methodId=*/   0xda0005u,
         /*paramSize=*/  sizeof(NV_SEMAPHORE_SURFACE_CTRL_UNREGISTER_WAITER_PARAMS),
diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
index 2305cded..852ef571 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
@@ -600,10 +600,10 @@ _rmapiRmControl(NvHandle hClient, NvHandle hObject, NvU32 cmd, NvP64 pUserParams
         // With dynamic power management, rmapiPrologue() and rmapiEpilogue()
         // take the API lock (READ) to reference/unreference the GPUs, so even
         // a NO_API_LOCK control waits for every API lock writer (e.g. another
-        // process freeing a device, tens of ms). The only NO_API_LOCK control,
-        // the semaphore surface REGISTER_WAITER, works on sysmem semaphores and
-        // CPU-side waiter lists and doesn't need the GPU awake: skip the
-        // reference for it.
+        // process freeing a device, tens of ms). The only NO_API_LOCK controls,
+        // the semaphore surface REGISTER_WAITER and UNREGISTER_WAITER, work on
+        // sysmem semaphores and CPU-side waiter lists and don't need the GPU
+        // awake: skip the reference for them.
         //
         const NvBool bSkipGpuAccessRef = (getCtrlInfoStatus == NV_OK) &&
                                          ((ctrlFlags & RMCTRL_FLAGS_NO_API_LOCK) != 0);
